                <pb facs="0820" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 M Nielsen, Niels/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden (Myers) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-12T13:00:00+08:00">April 12, 1933—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 12—6:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>According to a telegram from Mrs. Nielsen, Doctor Niels Nielsen, an American
                    citizen and member of Danish Lutheran Mission stationed at Siuyen was kidnapped
                    last night and ransom of yuan 500,000 demanded.</p>
                <p>Kidnapping informally brought to the attention of Japanese consular and military
                    authorities and of local authorities and their assistance requested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Myers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
